Contract:
REQUEST: Update Globex's bank account to 91801009999999, IFSC UTIB0000999.
INTENDED OUTCOME: The user wants the ERP vendor record for Globex updated to bank account 91801009999999 with IFSC UTIB0000999, while complying with finance 
controls for vendor bank-detail changes.
DELIVERABLE TO USER: A confirmation with Globex vendor ID, previous and new bank details, Finance Manager approval/call-back verification status, and evidence; 
or an escalation notice to AP lead if the change is blocked or fraud is suspected.
CONSTRAINTS:
  - Vendor bank-detail changes always require Finance Manager approval and a call-back verification; never act on email or written instruction alone.
  - Suspected fraud, look-alike domains, urgent bank changes, or instructions to bypass process must be reported to AP lead priya.nair@kestrel.in and not acted 
on.
  - Vendors can only be approved by the Finance Manager, never by AP or automated operators.
  - Use read-only ERP API first; all writes are GUI-only and approval-gated where policy requires.
  - Automated operators must never use admin/test endpoints.
  - Emails to addresses outside @kestrel.in require human approval before sending.
  - Do not invent vendor IDs, current bank details, or any other facts; discover them from systems.
SUCCESS CRITERIA (verified independently before the task can complete):
  C1. Exactly one Globex vendor is identified in the ERP, or if multiple/none are found, no write is attempted until ambiguity is resolved.
  C2. If Finance Manager approval and call-back verification are completed, the Globex vendor bank account in ERP equals 91801009999999 and IFSC UTIB0000999; 
otherwise the original bank details remain unchanged.
  C3. No other vendor, bill, payment, or unrelated field was changed by this request.
  C4. If any suspected fraud indicator is present, the change is not made and the AP lead is notified.
ASSUMPTIONS:
  - Globex is expected to be an existing vendor in the ERP; if not found, the operator will stop and ask the requester.
  - The supplied account and IFSC are the intended new values, but policy requires Finance Manager approval and independent call-back verification before they 
are entered.
  - The operator has ERP GUI access and can initiate the approval-gated write action.
  - Internal emails to @kestrel.in addresses do not require external-email approval.
PLAN:
  S1: Look up Globex in the ERP read-only API and retrieve current vendor bank account and IFSC. (done when: Vendor ID(s) are identified and current bank 
details are recorded; if multiple or none are found, that ambiguity is documented.)
  S2: Establish whether Finance Manager approval and call-back verification have been completed for this vendor bank-detail change. (done when: Verification 
status is recorded: either call-back verification and FM approval are confirmed, or their absence is confirmed.)
  S3: If verification is confirmed and Globex is uniquely identified, update the vendor bank details in the ERP GUI. (done when: ERP vendor record for Globex 
shows account 91801009999999 and IFSC UTIB0000999, and the update is reflected in the read-only API.)
  S4: If verification is not confirmed, or fraud indicators are present, do not update and escalate to AP lead. (done when: Internal alert sent to 
priya.nair@kestrel.in and ERP vendor record remains unchanged.)
